Models
------

mmBERT-small (https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/mmBERT-small), Johns Hopkins University CLSP. MIT License.
  The base of atelier-nano: its first layers and a trimmed vocabulary, fine-tuned by distillation.

Qwen3.5-0.8B (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B) and Qwen3.5-2B (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B),
Alibaba Cloud. Apache License 2.0.
  The bases of atelier-mini (0.8B in v0.4 and v0.5, 2B from v0.6). Changed: attention made non-causal, LoRA adapters trained by distillation and merged
  into the weights, a new readout; converted to GGUF and quantized.

pplx-decider-v1.3 and pplx-decider-flash-v1.3 (https://huggingface.co/perplexity-ai), Perplexity.
Apache License 2.0; derived from Qwen models.
  The teachers. Their answers are the labels the students learned from; none of their weights are in the students.

SigLIP 2 (https://huggingface.co/google/siglip2-base-patch16-256), Google. Apache License 2.0.
  The base of atelier-vision: its image tower and its text tower. Changed: LoRA adapters trained on this project's
  questions about pictures and merged into the weights; every layer's weights stored at 8 bits; the text tower's
  embedding table cut to the tokens of a trimmed vocabulary and stored at 4 bits; converted to ONNX.


