Pictures
--------

atelier-vision's pictures (the data/pictures.zip of each saved vision version) are of three kinds.

Photos from Open Images V7 (https://storage.googleapis.com/openimages/web/index.html), Google LLC. The labels and
image list are CC BY 4.0. The photos were published on Flickr by their authors under CC BY 2.0; each is kept as a
256 x 256 copy with its author, licence and page (photos.jsonl in the archive).

Buttons drawn from these icon sets, each under its own licence (their texts are in the archive's licences/ folder):
  Lucide (https://lucide.dev), Lucide Contributors. ISC License; parts from Feather, MIT License.
  Tabler Icons (https://tabler.io/icons), Paweł Kuna. MIT License.
  Bootstrap Icons (https://icons.getbootstrap.com), The Bootstrap Authors. MIT License.
  Heroicons (https://heroicons.com), Tailwind Labs. MIT License.
  Phosphor Icons (https://phosphoricons.com), Phosphor Icons. MIT License.
  Feather (https://feathericons.com), Cole Bemis. MIT License.
  Ionicons (https://ionic.io/ionicons), Ionic. MIT License.
  Material Design Icons (https://github.com/marella/material-design-icons, Google's icons), Google. Apache License 2.0.
  Octicons (https://primer.style/octicons), GitHub. MIT License.

Documents and pages drawn by vision/synth.py with made-up content: written for this project, CC BY 4.0. Pages and
some documents show photos from the Open Images set above where a site would have pictures.


Data
----

Text from these datasets is in the request pools and teacher labels (the data/ archives of each saved version).
The data/build_*.py scripts sampled, filtered and rewrote it into Atelier's decision requests, and the teachers
above labelled it.

MASSIVE (https://huggingface.co/datasets/AmazonScience/massive), Amazon. CC BY 4.0.
WildChat-1M (https://huggingface.co/datasets/allenai/WildChat-1M), Allen Institute for AI. ODC-BY 1.0.
Mind2Web (https://huggingface.co/datasets/osunlp/Mind2Web), The Ohio State University. CC BY 4.0.
glaive-function-calling-v2 (https://huggingface.co/datasets/glaiveai/glaive-function-calling-v2), Glaive AI.
  Apache License 2.0.
Synthetic-Persona-Chat (https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/Synthetic-Persona-Chat), Google. CC BY 4.0.
gliclass-v2.0 (https://huggingface.co/datasets/knowledgator/gliclass-v2.0), Knowledgator. Apache License 2.0.
synthetic_zeroshot_mixtral_v0.1 (https://huggingface.co/datasets/MoritzLaurer/synthetic_zeroshot_mixtral_v0.1),
  Moritz Laurer. Apache License 2.0.

COCO-35L (https://google.github.io/crossmodal-3600/), Google LLC. CC BY 4.0; captions of COCO
  (https://cocodataset.org, CC BY 4.0) translated by machine.
  A quarter of its dev split's captions in 21 languages, as text only: what atelier-vision's text tower is held to
  while it trains, and part of what its vocabulary is chosen from (data/questions.zip of each vision version).
Crossmodal-3600 (https://google.github.io/crossmodal-3600/), Google LLC. CC BY 4.0.
  Measures atelier-vision's search. Never trained on, and not in any archive here.
Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org), the Tatoeba contributors. CC BY 2.0 FR.
  Sentences in twelve languages decided which tokens atelier-vision's trimmed vocabulary keeps. No sentence is in
  any archive here.

The browser question families, the security building blocks and the natural inputs in data/gen, data/gen2,
data/gen3, data/gen4, data/gen4_src and data/security_src were written for this project by Claude (Anthropic) and
are part of the data licensed under CC BY 4.0 above. So are atelier-vision's tables and wordings: the things in
photos, the albums, the jobs of buttons, the kinds of document and the states of a page, each named in five
languages, and the templates questions about them are made from (vision/classes.py, icons.py, synth_words.py,
questions.py).
